{"type":"message","id":"5dc3365f","parentId":"97cbdf85","timestamp":"2026-02-11T22:22:36.450Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"! I can see that the NVIDIA model `stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash` is configured in the `providers` section under \"nvidia\". The configuration includes:\n- baseUrl: https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1\n- apiKey: (provided)\n- auth: api-key\n- models: includes stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash\n\nThe test script `test_models.py` already shows how to call the API. I can adapt that to specifically test the NVIDIA model with the message \"Hello, are you working?\". I could either:\n- Run the existing script and see if it tests that model (it tests all models in the config)\n- Write a custom script to test only that model and get the full response.\n\nBut the script only sends \"hi\" and prints status, not the response content. I need the actual model's response. So I need to modify it to capture and print the response content.\n\nI can create a simple Python script that uses the same config to send the specific message and print the model's response. I'll use the `exec` tool to run it, or I could just write a script and run it with exec.\n\nGiven the constraint to be concise, I'll create a temporary script that tests the NVIDIA model with the specific message and prints the response.\n\nI'll use the `write` tool to create a script, then `exec` to run it.\n\nLet's write a script: `test_nvidia_model.py` that does:\n- Load config from agents/ciel/models.json\n- Find the nvidia provider\n- For the model stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash, send a chat completion request with messages: [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello, are you working?\"}]\n- Print the model's response content.\n\nI'll include the imports: json, requests.\n\nI should be careful: the script should output only the response, maybe with some context.\n\nBetter: I'll write a script that prints a clear report.\n\nPlan:\n1. Write a Python script to /root/.openclaw/workspace/test_nvidia_model.py\n2. Execute it with `exec`, capturing stdout.\n3. Report the output.\n\nBut as a subagent, I can just run the script directly via exec. However, the script needs to be written first.\n\nI can also write a one-liner using Python -c, but it's easier to write a script.\n\nLet's proceed.\n\nI'll create the script with content.\n</think>\nI'll create a test script to query the NVIDIA model with the specific message."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_532b486d57b34f4c880966c0","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/test_nvidia_model.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport json\nimport requests\nimport sys\n\nconfig_path = \"/root/.openclaw/workspace/agents/ciel/models.json\"\nwith open(config_path) as f:\n    config = json.load(f)\n\nprovider = config[\"providers\"][\"nvidia\"]\nbase_url = provider[\"baseUrl\"].rstrip(\"/\")\napi_key = provider[\"apiKey\"]\nauth_type = provider.get(\"auth\", \"api-key\")\nmodels = provider[\"models\"]\n\n# Find the specific model\nmodel_id = \"stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash\"\nmodel_info = None\nfor m in models:\n    if m[\"id\"] == model_id:\n        model_info = m\n        break\n\nif not model_info:\n    print(f\"Model {model_id} not found in NVIDIA provider config\")\n    sys.exit(1)\n\nendpoint = f\"{base_url}/chat/completions\"\nheaders = {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}\nif auth_type == \"api-key\":\n    headers[\"Authorization\"] = f\"Bearer {api_key}\"\nelse:\n    headers[\"Authorization\"] = f\"{auth_type} {api_key}\"\n\npayload = {\n    \"model\": model_id,\n    \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello, are you working?\"}],\n    \"max_tokens\": 256,\n    \"stream\": False\n}\n\ntry:\n    resp = requests.post(endpoint, json=payload, headers=headers, timeout=30)\n    if resp.status_code == 200:\n        data = resp.json()\n        # Extract the assistant message content\n        if \"choices\" in data and len(data[\"choices\"]) > 0:\n            message = data